 :root-cause
 "The handwritten CLJ-to-generated-Java indexed conversion boundary invoked generated variant, destructor, and BigInteger methods without concrete type hints. Clojure therefore performed reflective method lookup on every generated drive/resume/scan round trip. The semantic model and opaque state were correct, but the trusted FFI boundary added avoidable allocation and latency."
 :fix
 "The indexed Java conversion boundary now statically dispatches generated initialization, step, resume, state, result, counter, projection, command, and numeric conversion calls. A compile-time reflection audit covers the complete indexed hot-boundary source span, and the public authority-mode benchmark separately gates latency, caller-thread allocation, and backend operations."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.characterization-fixture-test/generated-java-indexed-hot-boundary-is-reflection-free-test"
  "eacl.formal.authority-mode-benchmark/run-gate!"
  "formal mutation :generated-indexed-java-boundary-restores-reflection"]}
